verses.commentary:
112:5 In the OT, covenant brothers were to lend to the poor without interest (cf. Exod. 22:25; Lev. 25:35-38;
Deut. 15:7-8). To help the poor was a way to show one's devotion to YHWH, who cared for the poor (cf. Ps. 37:26;
Prov. 19:17; Matt. 5:42; Luke 6:35). The way one treats others clearly reveals his relationship with God (cf. Ps. 112:4).

112:6b Because of this line and Ps. 112:3b and 9b, an afterlife of some kind, not just the memory of God, is
implied! Heaven is not just God's memory but His people in fellowship with Him (cf. Matt. 22:31-32).

